"use strict";(Array.isArray(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs)?self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs:self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs=[]).push([[9417],{80906(e,t,r){e.exports=r.p+"assets/img/vendor-graph-setting-dashboard.ce18a43c.webp"},84261(e,t,r){r.r(t),r.d(t,{comp:()=>g,data:()=>h});var s=r(20641);const o=r.p+"assets/img/vendor-graph-setting-overview.daa6f4db.webp";var a=r(80906);const n=r.p+"assets/img/vendor-graph-setting-reports.acad8b5a.webp",i=r.p+"assets/img/vendor-graph-setting-transactions.b3976f23.webp",l=r.p+"assets/img/vendor-graph-setting-performance.3908ddd2.webp",c=r.p+"assets/img/vendor-graph-setting-products.3ad2f080.webp",d={},g=(0,r(66262).A)(d,[["render",function(e,t){return(0,s.uX)(),(0,s.CE)("div",null,t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,s.Fv)('<h1 id="graph-setting" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#graph-setting"><span>Graph Setting</span></a></h1><p>The <strong>Graph Setting</strong> page (<code>/seller/seller-graph-setting/</code>) allows vendors to personalize the appearance and visual styling of dashboard charts, analytics widgets, financial sparklines, and reporting graphs.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/vendor-graph-setting-overview.webp"><img src="'+o+'" alt="Vendor Graph Setting Cards Overview"></a></p><p>Vendors can navigate to this screen from the vendor panel menu under <strong>Settings → Graph Setting</strong>.</p><hr><h2 id="overview" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#overview"><span>Overview</span></a></h2><p>Marketplace vendors often rely on charts and graphs to quickly monitor their store performance, sales revenue, customer growth, and product catalog quality. With <strong>Graph Setting</strong>, each vendor can customize color palettes and chart types to fit their personal visual preferences or brand colors.</p><p>The Graph Setting hub organizes all customizable visual elements into five dedicated cards:</p><table><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">Section Card</th><th style="text-align:left;">Associated Endpoints</th><th style="text-align:center;">Total Graphs</th><th style="text-align:left;">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Dashboard</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>vendor-dashboard</code></td><td style="text-align:center;">15</td><td style="text-align:left;">Sales vs. commission, trends, customer comparisons, order statuses, country map, profile score, and stat card sparklines.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Reports</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>seller-reporting-sales</code>, <code>seller-reporting-products</code>, <code>seller-reporting-customers</code></td><td style="text-align:center;">10</td><td style="text-align:left;">Comprehensive reporting graphs for revenue, taxes, payment methods, units sold, and customer metrics.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Transactions</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>vendor-transactions</code></td><td style="text-align:center;">5</td><td style="text-align:left;">Micro sparkline graphs displayed across payout, withdrawal, and refund summary cards.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Performance</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>seller-account-health</code></td><td style="text-align:center;">1</td><td style="text-align:left;">The Account Health Score gauge meter and status thresholds.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Products</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>vendor-edit-product</code></td><td style="text-align:center;">1</td><td style="text-align:left;">The Listing Completeness progress bar displayed on the product edit screen.</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><h2 id="common-features-across-graph-setting-cards" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#common-features-across-graph-setting-cards"><span>Common Features Across Graph Setting Cards</span></a></h2><p>Each card page is designed with an intuitive two-column layout:</p><ul><li><strong>Left Column (Live Preview)</strong>: Displays an interactive, real-time preview of the actual card or chart widget as it appears in the seller panel.</li><li><strong>Right Column (Graph Settings)</strong>: Provides chart type selections and individual color pickers.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/vendor-graph-setting-dashboard.webp"><img src="'+a+'" alt="Vendor Graph Setting Dashboard Configuration"></a></p><h3 id="key-controls-actions" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#key-controls-actions"><span>Key Controls &amp; Actions:</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Chart Type Switcher</strong>: Choose your preferred data visualization mode where available (for example, <strong>Bar</strong>, <strong>Line</strong>, or <strong>Area</strong> for trend charts; <strong>Doughnut</strong>, <strong>Pie</strong>, or <strong>Bar</strong> for status breakdowns).</li><li><strong>Interactive Color Pickers</strong>: Click any color box to open the native color selector, or type any valid HEX color code directly.</li><li><strong>Default Color Label</strong>: Each color setting clearly displays its original default HEX value (e.g., <code>Default #a1b5f5</code>) for easy reference.</li><li><strong>Single Color Reset (<code>↻</code>)</strong>: Click the rotate icon button next to any color picker to instantly revert that single color back to its factory default without reloading the page.</li><li><strong>Save Changes</strong>: Click the primary <strong>Save Changes</strong> button at the bottom of the section to save your adjustments.</li><li><strong>Reset section to default</strong>: Click the ghost button to reset all chart styles and color pickers in that card back to their default theme settings after confirming the prompt.</li><li><strong>Back Button</strong>: Located at the top right of the page header to quickly return to the main Graph Setting hub.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="_1-dashboard-graphs" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-dashboard-graphs"><span>1. Dashboard Graphs</span></a></h2><p>Vendors can access this section by selecting <strong>Dashboard</strong> on the hub or visiting <code>/seller/seller-graph-setting/?wkmp_card=dashboard</code>.</p><p>This section controls the 15 visual elements shown on the main vendor dashboard:</p><h3 id="comparison-trend-charts" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#comparison-trend-charts"><span>Comparison &amp; Trend Charts</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Sales vs Commission</strong>: Compare gross sales volume against marketplace commission. Vendors can switch between <strong>Bar (default)</strong>, <strong>Line</strong>, and <strong>Area</strong> formats, and customize the <strong>Sales</strong> and <strong>Commission</strong> colors.</li><li><strong>Customers vs Orders</strong>: Track customer growth alongside order frequency using <strong>Bar (default)</strong>, <strong>Line</strong>, or <strong>Area</strong> layouts with separate colors for <strong>Customers</strong> and <strong>Orders</strong>.</li><li><strong>Trends: Sales</strong>: View daily, weekly, or monthly sales trajectories using <strong>Bar (default)</strong>, <strong>Line</strong>, or <strong>Area</strong> graphs.</li><li><strong>Trends: Orders</strong>: Monitor order count trends over time with customizable <strong>Bar (default)</strong>, <strong>Line</strong>, or <strong>Area</strong> representations.</li></ul><h3 id="order-status-distribution" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#order-status-distribution"><span>Order Status Distribution</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Order Status Chart</strong>: Displays the breakdown of store orders by fulfillment status.</li><li><strong>Supported Layouts</strong>: <strong>Doughnut (default)</strong>, <strong>Pie</strong>, or <strong>Bar</strong>.</li><li><strong>Customizable Status Colors</strong>: <ul><li><strong>Completed</strong> (Default <code>#34d298</code>)</li><li><strong>Pending</strong> (Default <code>#fdc700</code>)</li><li><strong>Processing</strong> (Default <code>#8ec5ff</code>)</li><li><strong>Cancelled</strong> (Default <code>#cad5e2</code>)</li><li><strong>Refunded</strong> (Default <code>#7c86ff</code>)</li><li><strong>Failed</strong> (Default <code>#ff6467</code>)</li><li><strong>Other statuses</strong> (Default <code>#dddddd</code>)</li></ul></li></ul><h3 id="geographic-profile-analytics" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#geographic-profile-analytics"><span>Geographic &amp; Profile Analytics</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Top Billing Countries Map</strong>: Interactive world map illustrating where store orders originate. Vendors can configure: <ul><li><strong>With sales</strong>: Highlight color for countries generating orders (Default <code>#0a0a0a</code>).</li><li><strong>Without sales</strong>: Base land color for countries without orders (Default <code>#f5f5f5</code>).</li></ul></li><li><strong>Profile Score</strong>: Circular arc meter showing vendor profile completion percentage: <ul><li><strong>Score Progress</strong>: Arc indicator fill color (Default <code>#a1b5f5</code>).</li><li><strong>Track Background</strong>: Arc background circle color (Default <code>#ebebeb</code>).</li></ul></li></ul><h3 id="stat-card-sparklines-8-metric-cards" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#stat-card-sparklines-8-metric-cards"><span>Stat Card Sparklines (8 Metric Cards)</span></a></h3><p>Each summary card at the top of the vendor dashboard contains a subtle sparkline curve:</p><ul><li><strong>Total Sales</strong>: Sparkline stroke color.</li><li><strong>Total Orders</strong>: Sparkline stroke color.</li><li><strong>Total Customers</strong>: Sparkline stroke color.</li><li><strong>Average Order Sell</strong>: Sparkline stroke color.</li><li><strong>Total Payout</strong>: Sparkline stroke color.</li><li><strong>Remaining Payout</strong>: Sparkline stroke color.</li><li><strong>Customer Feedback</strong>: Sparkline stroke color.</li><li><strong>Account Health</strong>: Sparkline stroke color.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="_2-reports-graphs" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-reports-graphs"><span>2. Reports Graphs</span></a></h2><p>Vendors can access this section by selecting <strong>Reports</strong> on the hub or visiting <code>/seller/seller-graph-setting/?wkmp_card=reports</code>.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/vendor-graph-setting-reports.webp"><img src="'+n+'" alt="Vendor Graph Setting Reports Configuration"></a></p><p>This section controls 10 charts used across the marketplace sales, product, and customer analytics screens:</p><ul><li><strong>Sales Reporting (Revenue &amp; Volumes)</strong>: <ul><li><strong>Total Sales</strong>: Line, Bar, or Area representation for overall store revenue.</li><li><strong>Total Commission</strong>: Line, Bar, or Area tracking of vendor commission earnings.</li><li><strong>Total Orders</strong>: Line, Bar, or Area chart of placed customer orders.</li><li><strong>Average Order Value (AOV)</strong>: Line, Bar, or Area chart tracking basket spend over time.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Taxes &amp; Payment Insights</strong>: <ul><li><strong>Tax Collected</strong>: Line, Bar, or Area chart for sales tax amounts.</li><li><strong>Top Tax Rates</strong>: Doughnut, Pie, or Bar chart displaying distribution by applied tax bracket.</li><li><strong>Refunds</strong>: Line, Bar, or Area visualization of order refund volume.</li><li><strong>Top Payment Methods</strong>: Doughnut, Pie, or Bar chart detailing customer payment gateway usage.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Product &amp; Customer Analytics</strong>: <ul><li><strong>Products Reporting (Units Sold)</strong>: Line, Bar, or Area graph showing quantity of product items sold.</li><li><strong>Customers Reporting (Total Customers)</strong>: Line, Bar, or Area graph tracking repeat and new customer acquisition.</li></ul></li></ul><hr><h2 id="_3-transactions-graphs" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-transactions-graphs"><span>3. Transactions Graphs</span></a></h2><p>Vendors can access this section by selecting <strong>Transactions</strong> on the hub or visiting <code>/seller/seller-graph-setting/?wkmp_card=transactions</code>.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/vendor-graph-setting-transactions.webp"><img src="'+i+'" alt="Vendor Graph Setting Transactions Configuration"></a></p><p>The transactions page (<code>vendor-transactions</code>) provides financial summaries for seller earnings and withdrawal requests. Vendors can configure the sparkline stroke color (Default <code>#00a63e</code>) for each card:</p><ul><li><strong>Total Earning</strong>: Sparkline for lifetime net earnings accumulated.</li><li><strong>Total Withdraw</strong>: Sparkline for funds successfully withdrawn to the vendor bank or payment account.</li><li><strong>Total Pending Withdraw</strong>: Sparkline for withdrawal requests currently under admin review.</li><li><strong>Total Refunded</strong>: Sparkline for payments deducted due to customer refunds.</li><li><strong>Last Withdraw</strong>: Sparkline tracking the most recent payout disbursement.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="_4-performance-graphs" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-performance-graphs"><span>4. Performance Graphs</span></a></h2><p>Vendors can access this section by selecting <strong>Performance</strong> on the hub or visiting <code>/seller/seller-graph-setting/?wkmp_card=performance</code>.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/vendor-graph-setting-performance.webp"><img src="'+l+'" alt="Vendor Graph Setting Performance Health Score Configuration"></a></p><p>This section customizes the visual gauge for the vendor&#39;s <strong>Account Health Score</strong> (<code>seller-account-health</code>):</p><ul><li><strong>Health Gauge Segments</strong>: <ul><li><strong>Unhealthy</strong> (Default <code>#f43f5e</code>): Represents low performance scores requiring immediate attention.</li><li><strong>At Risk</strong> (Default <code>#fdc700</code>): Represents borderline performance scores.</li><li><strong>Healthy</strong> (Default <code>#34d298</code>): Represents high compliance and solid store operational standing.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Marker Color</strong> (Default <code>#0a0a0a</code>): Controls the needle marker that points to the vendor&#39;s calculated score on the gauge meter.</li></ul><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Live Score Calculator</p><p>The colors chosen in this section are also shared by the interactive score calculation breakdown in the &quot;How is this calculated?&quot; guide on the vendor account health page.</p></div><hr><h2 id="_5-products-graphs-listing-completeness" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-products-graphs-listing-completeness"><span>5. Products Graphs (Listing Completeness)</span></a></h2><p>Vendors can access this section by selecting <strong>Products</strong> on the hub or visiting <code>/seller/seller-graph-setting/?wkmp_card=products</code>.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/vendor-graph-setting-products.webp"><img src="'+c+'" alt="Vendor Graph Setting Products Listing Completeness Configuration"></a></p><p>This section controls the visual styling of the <strong>Listing Completeness</strong> progress bar:</p><ul><li><strong>Filled Color</strong> (Default <code>#34d298</code>): The active progress fill showing the current completeness percentage.</li><li><strong>Track Color</strong> (Default <code>#ebebeb</code>): The background track representing remaining uncompleted product details.</li></ul><h3 id="how-it-works-on-the-product-edit-page" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-it-works-on-the-product-edit-page"><span>How It Works on the Product Edit Page:</span></a></h3><ul><li>When a vendor creates or edits a product (<code>vendor-edit-product</code>), the <strong>Listing Completeness</strong> card appears near the top of the form.</li><li>The progress bar dynamically calculates the product completeness score (e.g., 35%, 60%, 100%) based on vital fields like product title, featured image, categories, price, short description, and attributes.</li><li>Vendors can expand the missing details checklist to see exactly which fields need attention to optimize their product visibility in marketplace search and category filters.</li><li>The colors customized in <strong>Graph Setting → Products</strong> reflect directly on this progress bar across all product edit screens.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="summary-of-graph-settings-workflow" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#summary-of-graph-settings-workflow"><span>Summary of Graph Settings Workflow</span></a></h2><ol><li>Navigate to <strong>Settings → Graph Setting</strong> from the vendor sidebar menu.</li><li>Select the card section you wish to customize: <strong>Dashboard</strong>, <strong>Reports</strong>, <strong>Transactions</strong>, <strong>Performance</strong>, or <strong>Products</strong>.</li><li>Choose your preferred <strong>Chart Type</strong> (Bar, Line, Area, Doughnut, Pie) for supported graphs.</li><li>Select desired hues using the <strong>Color Pickers</strong>, or click the <strong>Reset (<code>↻</code>)</strong> button next to any color to revert it individually.</li><li>Click <strong>Save Changes</strong> at the bottom of the page to apply the updates immediately.</li><li>To restore an entire card back to default settings at any time, click <strong>Reset section to default</strong> and confirm the prompt.</li></ol>',59)]))}]]),h=JSON.parse('{"path":"/documentation/vendor-graph-setting.html","title":"Graph Setting – Vendor / Seller Guide","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Graph Setting – Vendor / Seller Guide","description":"Learn how to customize chart types, color schemes, and visual analytics palettes across your vendor dashboard, reports, transactions, and product management tools in WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace."},"headers":[{"level":2,"title":"Overview","slug":"overview","link":"#overview","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Common Features Across Graph Setting Cards","slug":"common-features-across-graph-setting-cards","link":"#common-features-across-graph-setting-cards","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Key Controls & Actions:","slug":"key-controls-actions","link":"#key-controls-actions","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"1. Dashboard Graphs","slug":"_1-dashboard-graphs","link":"#_1-dashboard-graphs","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Comparison & Trend Charts","slug":"comparison-trend-charts","link":"#comparison-trend-charts","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Order Status Distribution","slug":"order-status-distribution","link":"#order-status-distribution","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Geographic & Profile Analytics","slug":"geographic-profile-analytics","link":"#geographic-profile-analytics","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Stat Card Sparklines (8 Metric Cards)","slug":"stat-card-sparklines-8-metric-cards","link":"#stat-card-sparklines-8-metric-cards","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"2. Reports Graphs","slug":"_2-reports-graphs","link":"#_2-reports-graphs","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"3. Transactions Graphs","slug":"_3-transactions-graphs","link":"#_3-transactions-graphs","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"4. Performance Graphs","slug":"_4-performance-graphs","link":"#_4-performance-graphs","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"5. Products Graphs (Listing Completeness)","slug":"_5-products-graphs-listing-completeness","link":"#_5-products-graphs-listing-completeness","children":[{"level":3,"title":"How It Works on the Product Edit Page:","slug":"how-it-works-on-the-product-edit-page","link":"#how-it-works-on-the-product-edit-page","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Summary of Graph Settings Workflow","slug":"summary-of-graph-settings-workflow","link":"#summary-of-graph-settings-workflow","children":[]}],"git":{},"filePathRelative":"documentation/vendor-graph-setting.md"}')}}]);